meta {
  name: AgentForge Clinical Co-Pilot
}

docs {
  # AgentForge Clinical Co-Pilot API collection

  Runs the same handshake the panel performs (ARCHITECTURE.md, "Agent HTTP API
  and the Runnable Collection"): log in to OpenEMR, open a chart, get the
  co-pilot CSRF token, start a conversation bound to that chart, mint a
  per-turn ticket, and call the agent. Then the use-case turns, the failure
  examples, and health and readiness.

  Run in order (folders 1 to 4). The pre-request script on every turn request
  mints a fresh ticket automatically. Select the `local` or `deployed`
  environment and set the credentials variables there (never commit them).

  CLI:  bru run docs/api-collection --env deployed --env-var DEMO_PASSWORD=...
}
